    "title": "WWE WrestleMania 42: Start Time, Date & How to Watch",
    "text": "Started in 1984, WrestleMania is WWE’s biggest show of the year. It has long been recognized as the stage where legends—like Hulk Hogan, “Stone Cold” Steve Austin, and The Undertaker—are made. With WrestleMania 42 fast approaching, the event returns to Las Vegas for the second consecutive year.For most of its history, WrestleMania was a one-night event. In recent years, however, it has evolved into a two-night spectacle.AdvertisementWrestleMania 42 takes place across Saturday, April 18 and Sunday, April 19, 2026, with both nights beginning at 6:00 p.m. ET.Here’s everything you need to know about start times and how to watch live.Roman Reigns will compete in his 11th WrestleMania main event at WrestleMania 42.Getty ImagesWhat Time Does WrestleMania Start?WrestleMania begins at 6:00 p.m. ET on both nights. That’s 5:00 p.m. CT and 3:00 p.m. PT—the local time in Las Vegas.Rhea Ripley will challenge Jade Cargill for the WWE Women's Championship at WrestleMania 42.Getty ImagesRelated: Every WrestleMania 42 Match Ranked From Least to Most AnticipatedPat McAfee will be in Randy Orton's corner against Cody Rhodes at WrestleMania 42.Getty ImagesWrestleMania will stream exclusively on ESPN’s new platform this year following WWE’s move away from Peacock, as part of a new partnership bringing all Premium Live Events to the service.AdvertisementTo watch WrestleMania, you can:Download the ESPN app and subscribe to ESPN Unlimited (starting at $29.99/month)Bundle ESPN with Disney+ and Hulu (starting at $35.99/month)Sign in with an eligible live TV providerSupported providers include DIRECTV, FuboTV, Hulu + Live TV, Spectrum, and Verizon FiOS.Here’s Cody Rhodes explaining how to watch WrestleMania 42 on the ESPN app:The first hour of WrestleMania Saturday will air on ESPN2 for viewers with a live TV provider, featuring a Six-Man Tag Team Match involving Logan Paul and IShowSpeed as the opening bout.The first hour of WrestleMania Sunday will air on ESPN, headlined by a highly anticipated generational clash between Brock Lesnar and rising WWE star Oba Femi.AdvertisementRelated: Related StoriesRelated: The Reason CM Punk Called Out Pat McAfee's Agent on WWE RawThis story was originally published by Athlon Sports on Apr 11, 2026, where it first appeared in the Wrestling section. Add Athlon Sports as a Preferred Source by clicking here.",
